774 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 563 0 R
/E (The origins of the university can be traced back to the Federal Government Urdu College, which was established in 1949 by Baba-e-Urdu, Maulvi Abdul Haq, a leading figure in the promotion of the Urdu language. This institution played a pioneering role in advocating for Urdu as a medium of instruction in higher education. Over time, it evolved into a full-fledged university, reflecting the growing demand for accessible education that integrates national identity with academic excellence.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
775 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 563 0 R
/E (FUUAST offers undergraduate, graduate, and postgraduate programs in fields such as natural sciences, social sciences, humanities, business administration, computer science, and education. The university is structured into various faculties and departments, each committed to fostering critical thinking, research skills, and intellectual growth. By combining traditional knowledge with modern academic approaches, FUUAST aims to prepare students to meet the challenges of a rapidly changing global environment.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
776 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 563 0 R
/E (A distinctive feature of the university is its emphasis on Urdu as a language of instruction, particularly in disciplines where English has traditionally dominated. This approach not only facilitates learning for students from diverse linguistic backgrounds but also contributes to the development of academic literature in Urdu. At the same time, the university ensures that students are equipped with proficiency in English and other necessary skills to compete internationally.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
777 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 563 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
778 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 563 0 R
/E (In addition to academic excellence, FUUAST places strong emphasis on character building, social responsibility, and civic engagement. Through extracurricular activities, student societies, and community outreach programs, the university nurtures well-rounded individuals who can contribute positively to society. Its inclusive environment promotes diversity, tolerance, and mutual respect among students from different cultural and socioeconomic backgrounds.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
