<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 572 0 R
/E (The contemporary international system is experiencing a profound transformation characterized by the emergence of multipolarity, evolving geopolitical alignments, and the growing importance of regional cooperation. In this dynamic global environment, relations between Russia and Pakistan have entered a promising phase marked by mutual trust, pragmatic engagement, and expanding areas of cooperation. Both countries are increasingly viewing each other as constructive partners in promoting regional stability, economic development, and inclusive connectivity across Eurasia and South Asia. While historical circumstances limited close interaction during the Cold War, Russia and Pakistan have, in recent years, successfully moved beyond legacy constraints to develop a relationship based on shared interests and complementary strengths. Cooperation has expanded in key areas such as defense dialogue, energy collaboration, trade, education, regional connectivity, and coordination on regional security challenges. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
