1047 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 581 0 R
/T (The development of a polycentric world order is changing the usual approaches to international security, increasing the weight of regional alliances. In this context, Russia's and Pakistan's cooperation within the Shanghai Cooperation Organization takes on a special significance, as bilateral relations are gradually establishing a stable institutional foundation for security. This process aligns with the common challenges faced by the region. Additionally, it highlights the shift from fragmented negotiations to joint action. Pakistan's accession to the SCO in 2017 has significantly revitalized ties between Moscow and Islamabad. During the Cold War, the countries were on opposite sides of the geopolitical confrontation. Today, their rapprochement is based on their shared interests in maintaining stability in Central and South Asia. Within the SCO, both countries actively participate in the Regional Anti-Terrorist Structure, coordinate measures against terrorism, extremism, and separatism, exchange intelligence, and engage in joint efforts.)
/E (The development of a polycentric world order is changing the usual approaches to international security, increasing the weight of regional alliances. In this context, Russia's and Pakistan's cooperation within the Shanghai Cooperation Organization takes on a special significance, as bilateral relations are gradually establishing a stable institutional foundation for security. This process aligns with the common challenges faced by the region. Additionally, it highlights the shift from fragmented negotiations to joint action. Pakistan's accession to the SCO in 2017 has significantly revitalized ties between Moscow and Islamabad. During the Cold War, the countries were on opposite sides of the geopolitical confrontation. Today, their rapprochement is based on their shared interests in maintaining stability in Central and South Asia. Within the SCO, both countries actively participate in the Regional Anti-Terrorist Structure, coordinate measures against terrorism, extremism, and separatism, exchange intelligence, and engage in joint efforts.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [4]
>>
