1184 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 590 0 R
/E (Seema Azeem is a third-year PhD candidate at the Institute of Education, Higher School of Economics, Moscow, Russia, and serves as a Lecturer in Baluchistan, Pakistan. Her research centers on school climate, with particular attention to the psychological and social dimensions of schooling as experienced by principals, teachers, and students. She examines how different leadership styles shape institutional culture, student well-being, and behavioral outcomes within diverse and often under-resourced contexts. Through her work, Seema seeks to generate evidence-based insights that inform leadership practices and contribute to more inclusive and supportive school environments. She is especially interested in understanding how leadership can foster safety, relationships between different stakeholders of the school and academic resilience. Her engagement in international conferences reflects her commitment to scholarly dialogue, comparative perspectives, and collaborative research aimed at strengthening educational leadership and school climate globally.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
