<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 605 0 R
/E (Vasily Stepanovich Khristoforov, Corresponding Member of the Russian Academy of Sciences, Doctor of Law, Professor, Director of the Institute of International Relations and Political Science at the Russian State University for the Humanities, Senior Researcher at the N.A. Dobrolyubov Nizhny Novgorod State Linguistic University. Research interests: leading specialist in the field of political and military history of Russia in the 20th-21st centuries; history of the countries of the Middle East and Central Asia; oriental studies, international relations, international security, history of domestic intelligence and counterintelligence. The author of more than 300 scientific papers published in leading scientific journals in Russia and abroad \(Austria, Hungary, Germany, Italy, Kazakhstan, China, Poland, Finland\), including 12 monographs \(Khristoforov V.S. Military campaigns of the USSR and the USA in Afghanistan: a comparative analysis. Moscow, 2025; Ibid. Soviet special services open the East. Moscow, 2019; Ibid. Afghanistan: the military-political presence of the USSR 1979-1989. Moscow, 2016 and others\), as well as scientific articles published in journals included in the White List, the HAC list, the Web of Science and Scopus databases.)
/Pg 56 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
