/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 607 0 R
/E (A Candidate of Historical Sciences and Associate Professor at the Chair of International Relations, World Politics and Diplomacy, she is affiliated with the Institute of International Relations, History and Oriental Studies at Kazan Federal University. Her academic work focuses on international relations, global political dynamics, and diplomatic studies, with particular emphasis on historical perspectives in world politics. She has contributed to teaching and research in areas such as foreign policy analysis, regional studies, and international cooperation. With a strong commitment to academic excellence, she actively engages in scholarly activities, including research publications, conferences, and collaborative projects. Her work reflects a deep understanding of global affairs and a dedication to advancing knowledge in the field of international relations.)
/Pg 58 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
