/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 613 0 R
/E (Syed Ehsan Ali is a Lecturer in International Relations at the Federal Urdu University of Arts, Sciences & Technology \(FUUAST\), Islamabad. He holds an MPhil in American Studies and a BS \(Hons\) in Political Science from Quaid-i-Azam University, Islamabad. His research focuses on great power competition, South Asian politics, and Eurasian geopolitics. He has published in various national and international journals on topics including US-China rivalry, the regional implications of the QUAD, and Indo-Pacific security dynamics. Previously, he served as a Young Parliamentary Associate at the Senate of Pakistan under an EU-funded program, where he contributed to policy research and parliamentary initiatives. His current research examines Pakistan-Russia relations within an emerging polycentric international order, with particular emphasis on soft balancing and regional security frameworks, contributing to contemporary debates on global and regional strategic transformations.)
/Pg 64 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
