/E (Saima Azhar is a faculty member at the Federal Urdu University of Arts, Sciences & Technology \(FUUAST\), where she has been teaching and conducting research in Pakistan Studies and International Relations since 2015. She is currently pursuing her PhD, with a research focus on climate security and environmental governance. Her academic work examines the intersection of climate change, security, and regional cooperation, with particular emphasis on emerging challenges in environmental sustainability and policy responses. She has published numerous research papers in national and international journals and has presented her work at various international conferences. In addition to her academic responsibilities, she is actively engaged in policy research and analysis, contributing to discussions on climate diplomacy, environmental sustainability, and regional security frameworks. Her current research explores climate security within the broader context of evolving global and regional governance structures.)
/Pg 65 0 R
/K [1]
