/E (r. Faisal Javaid is Head of the Department of International Relations and Mass Communication and Deputy Director at the Office of Research Innovation and Commercialization \(ORIC\) at the Federal Urdu University of Arts, Science & Technology \(FUUAST\), Islamabad, where he has been teaching since 2009. His research focuses on the foreign relations of Central Asia, with particular emphasis on regional connectivity between Pakistan, Central Asia, and the Russian Federation. He is the author of Bridging Horizons: Unraveling the Enigma of Connectivity between Pakistan and Central Asia \(IPS, 2024\) and editor of New World Order: In Statu Nascendi \(FNCA, Poland, 2024\), in addition to contributing to several scholarly volumes. He serves as Senior Vice President \(Honorary\) of the Consortium for Asia Pacific and Eurasian Studies \(CAPES\). A postdoctoral fellow of the Harriman Institute, Columbia University, Dr. Javaid has published over thirty-three research papers, presented widely at international forums, and served as a Visiting Professor in Poland. He is an active member of ISA, IPSA, MPSA, and APT.)
/Pg 68 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
