1645 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 620 0 R
/T (This research examines the growing connectivity between Central Asia, Russia, and Pakistan, focusing on its strategic relevance for fostering deeper regional economic integration across Eurasia. It explores how historical trade routes, revived under contemporary geopolitical and economic imperatives, are being reimagined through initiatives such as the China-Pakistan Economic Corridor, the International North-South Transport Corridor, and regional transport and energy infrastructure projects. It identifies persistent challenges hindering connectivity, including fragile political environments, infrastructural bottlenecks, external strategic rivalries, and prevailing security threats. Moreover, through the analytical lenses of Regionalism and Geoeconomics, the research examines how economic and political motivations are converging to reshape regional alignments.)
/E (This research examines the growing connectivity between Central Asia, Russia, and Pakistan, focusing on its strategic relevance for fostering deeper regional economic integration across Eurasia. It explores how historical trade routes, revived under contemporary geopolitical and economic imperatives, are being reimagined through initiatives such as the China-Pakistan Economic Corridor, the International North-South Transport Corridor, and regional transport and energy infrastructure projects. It identifies persistent challenges hindering connectivity, including fragile political environments, infrastructural bottlenecks, external strategic rivalries, and prevailing security threats. Moreover, through the analytical lenses of Regionalism and Geoeconomics, the research examines how economic and political motivations are converging to reshape regional alignments.)
/Pg 71 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
