1726 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 625 0 R
/T (A characteristic of the development of the modern global economy is the gradual and relatively stable division of countries into core capitalist economies and peripheral economies. While industrial production processes gradually shifted, in terms of location and growth of economic efficiency, to countries with cheap labor and economic resources, core capitalist countries have made the development of innovation, the development and sale of new technological solutions and production methods on the global market, the foundation of their economic systems. The globalization processes occurring in the global economy in recent decades have only intensified this trend.Nevertheless, a number of new centers of innovation, scientific, and financial development worldwide demonstrate that peripheral countries are aware of the current situation and are taking steps to change it. The development and formation of new innovation centers requires government action within the framework of national economic and innovation policies. However, existing and growing trends toward regionalization in the global economic system demonstrate that the combined efforts of countries to create conditions for the development of new technological solutions \(within groups of countries\) are proving most effective.In accordance with the above, it is important to consider that innovative interaction requires both collaboration between innovative and manufacturing organizations and cooperation between countries through the establishment of links between scientific and educational systems. Accordingly, cooperation in scientific and educational spheres becomes the foundation for future innovative interaction.Innovative interaction between the economic systems of the Russian Federation and Pakistan can only be based on the establishment of information \(communication\) links between scientific, educational, financial, and manufacturing structures. Each level of this systemic interaction is important, both within regional economic systems and at the level of national economies as a whole. Selecting priority areas of interaction, taking into account the scientific and financial capabilities of the two countries, requires analyzing and forecasting various options.)
/E (A characteristic of the development of the modern global economy is the gradual and relatively stable division of countries into core capitalist economies and peripheral economies. While industrial production processes gradually shifted, in terms of location and growth of economic efficiency, to countries with cheap labor and economic resources, core capitalist countries have made the development of innovation, the development and sale of new technological solutions and production methods on the global market, the foundation of their economic systems. The globalization processes occurring in the global economy in recent decades have only intensified this trend.Nevertheless, a number of new centers of innovation, scientific, and financial development worldwide demonstrate that peripheral countries are aware of the current situation and are taking steps to change it. The development and formation of new innovation centers requires government action within the framework of national economic and innovation policies. However, existing and growing trends toward regionalization in the global economic system demonstrate that the combined efforts of countries to create conditions for the development of new technological solutions \(within groups of countries\) are proving most effective.In accordance with the above, it is important to consider that innovative interaction requires both collaboration between innovative and manufacturing organizations and cooperation between countries through the establishment of links between scientific and educational systems. Accordingly, cooperation in scientific and educational spheres becomes the foundation for future innovative interaction.Innovative interaction between the economic systems of the Russian Federation and Pakistan can only be based on the establishment of information \(communication\) links between scientific, educational, financial, and manufacturing structures. Each level of this systemic interaction is important, both within regional economic systems and at the level of national economies as a whole. Selecting priority areas of interaction, taking into account the scientific and financial capabilities of the two countries, requires analyzing and forecasting various options.)
/Pg 76 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
