/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 627 0 R
/E ( Preliminary findings suggest that while Arctic routes present theoretical opportunities for reducing transit times and costs between Pakistan and Russian ports, practical barriers, including infrastructure limitations, insurance costs, regulatory uncertainties, and geopolitical risks, significantly constrain immediate commercial viability. The study identifies niche opportunities in specific sectors and seasonal windows, while recognizing that Pakistan-Russia trade dynamics remain primarily shaped by geopolitical considerations rather than purely economic optimization. The research contributes to broader debates on how climate-induced transformations in distant regions create ripple effects across global trade networks and bilateral relationships, demonstrating that Arctic change is not merely a regional phenomenon but a catalyst for reconfiguring international economic and strategic partnerships.)
/Pg 78 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
