/E (Dr. Fizza Batool is an Assistant Professor at SZABIST University, Karachi, specializing in comparative politics with a particular focus on populism, democratization, and South Asian political dynamics. Her research explores the evolving nature of political institutions, leadership patterns, and democratic transitions in the region. She has contributed to academic discourse through her engagement with global research communities and policy-oriented institutions. In recognition of her scholarly work, she was awarded prestigious research fellowships at the Central European University Democracy Institute in Budapest in 2024 and the Stimson Center in Washington, D.C. in 2020. These experiences have enriched her comparative perspective and strengthened her analytical approach to contemporary political challenges. Dr. Batool is committed to advancing critical research and fostering academic excellence through teaching, mentorship, and collaborative inquiry in the field of political science.)
/Pg 79 0 R
/K [2]
>>
