/E (Dr. Sidra Khan is an Assistant Professor of International Relations at Bahria University, Karachi. She holds a PhD in International Relations from Quaid-e-Azam University, Islamabad. Her teaching and research focus on U.S. foreign policy, South Asian security, strategic alliances, conflict resolution, and global governance, with a particular emphasis on Global South perspectives. Dr. Khan has published extensively in leading academic and policy-oriented journals on topics such as great power politics, regional security dynamics, the Kashmir issue, and evolving global orders. She has presented her research at numerous national and international conferences and actively engages with policy think tanks, including ISSRA, SVI, and CSCR. Beyond academia, she contributes to public discourse as a television host and guest expert, offering insights on international security and geopolitical developments. Her work bridges academic research, policy analysis, and media engagement.)
/Pg 83 0 R
/K [1]
>>
