<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 638 0 R
/E (Dr. Lubna Sunawar is a scholar of Peace and Conflict Studies, specializing in international security, radicalization, post-conflict peacebuilding, and the role of emerging technologies in global politics. Her research critically examines the intersection of structural violence, relative deprivation, and extremism, with a regional focus on fragile and conflict-affected states such as Afghanistan, Iraq, Somalia, and Yemen. She has developed innovative theoretical contributions, including the Deprivation Radicalization Escalation Model \(DREM\), and incorporates AI-driven discourse analysis and geospatial mapping into conflict research. Her work reflects a strong interdisciplinary approach, combining theory with methodological innovation. Dr. Sunawar has presented at international conferences and contributes to discussions on climate-induced migration, human rights, and the ethical use of technology in education and security governance. She is also actively engaged in curriculum development, linking international relations theory with contemporary global challenges)
/Pg 89 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
