/E (Ms. Khushboo Farid Khan Ghouri is a Lecturer at FAST-NUCES \(National University of Computer and Emerging Sciences\), Pakistan, and a PhD Fellow at the Department of International Relations, University of Karachi. She has over six years of teaching and research experience in higher education, with academic expertise in strategic studies, Nuclear Studies, emerging technologies, cybersecurity, gender studies, human rights, and global power politics. Her doctoral research examines the impact of emerging technologies on future great power competition, while her MPhil work focused on cyberspace as a domain of power and competitiveness in international relations. She has published extensively in peer-reviewed national and international journals and has contributed to IEEE-indexed conference proceedings and edited volumes. Ms. Ghouri actively participates in international academic forums and is a member of the Midwest Political Science Association and Center for Alternative Perspectives. Her work bridges academic research, policy relevance, and interdisciplinary inquiry in contemporary international relations and discourse.)
/Pg 93 0 R
/K [1]
>>
