2078 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 647 0 R
/E (The recent shift in geopolitics and geoeconomics has resulted in new global alignments, with middle powers becoming more significant in shaping regional importance. This shifting dynamic reflects a broader crisis in the existing world order, moving from unipolarity to multipolarity. Pakistan located in a central position of powers, is significantly inflicted by these changes. Earlier, Pakistan have had remained aligned with the US, however, with fluctuations in the US-Pak ties. Hence, it is high time for Pakistan to reconsider the ties with US and look for alternative ways for its economic growth through engaging its partnership with new emerging powers like; China, Russia and the Middle Eastern countries, particularly amid shifting US priorities. Pakistan lies in a geostrategic position on the globe, providing a connecting energy route to Gulf countries with East Asia and Europe. Owing to the geographic route, Russia and Pakistan have signed economic deals, strategic deals amid the new power dynamics in the region. The current research focuses on Pakistan-Russia relations through the lens of Regional Security Complex Theory \(RSCT\) which identifies a group of states whose primary national security issues are strongly correlate d that they cannot be addressed independently. The theory views security interdependence as a key element in the creation of geographic groups. Since the post Ukraine Russia war, Pakistan is engaging with Russia through energy deals, security ties, and cultural exchanges programs driven by mutual interest. The researcher aims to examine the risks and opportunities for Pakistan and Russia economic and diplomatic relations aligned with the objectives of promoting sustainable economic growth and decent work through strategic collaboration)
/Pg 98 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
