/P 649 0 R
/E (UNESCO's cultural heritage sites vastly outweigh natural heritage sites; this study criticizes this imbalance and argues that it would be better if the opposite were true, given the global threat of climate change. The threats to natural heritage sites, particularly in vulnerable regions, caused by climate change are considered, along with numerous arguments that the conservation of natural heritage sites actually benefits cultural heritage sites in the long term from the extreme negative impacts of climate change if the opposite were done. UNESCO's emphasis on selecting natural heritage sites over cultural heritage sites is driven by various published documents. UNESCO's emphasis on selecting natural heritage sites over cultural heritage sites is driven by various published documents. Climate change is a phenomenon that must be taken into account before taking any action in our time. UNESCO plays a vital role in addressing this global emergency, and protecting natural heritage sites can be of great help in ensuring the future of the planet and its people.)
/Pg 100 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
