2162 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 652 0 R
/E (This paper makes the case that in light of regional security concerns and global multipolarity, Pakistan-Russia relations are entering an interest-driven phase. Both nations had a distrustful relationship during Cold War because of their competing interests. However, in recent years, the two countries' relations have been steadily improving. The convergence of diplomacy, economics, security, and cultural connectedness is becoming more and more necessary for a durable geopolitical alliance. Language plays a pivotal role in enhancing international relations by enhancing communication, cultural connectedness and diplomacy. Promoting a foreign language like Russian language in Pakistan can be effective strategy for improving bilateral ties with Russia. The strategy for such promotion includes academic exchanges, tourism and people-to-people connectivity which can project Russian identity and culture among its population. Soft power activities are crucial to build mutual understanding and long-term trust. The primary finding of this study is the significance of Russian language in the development of Pak-Russia relations. In order to improve Pakistan-Russia ties, this study examines Russian language training centers, institutions, cultural exchange initiatives and their future prospects in Pakistan. The Communication Theory framework used in this study highlights the significance of good communication in influencing interactions between states and other players. Its main notion is that diplomacy requires human connection to build trustworthy partnerships. This study investigates how promoting Russian throughout Pakistan can improve Pak-Russia relations. This study employs bibliometric and content analysis as its methodology to find trends and patterns in language-international relations research.)
/Pg 103 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
