/E (Amara Amir is a legal academia from Pakistan with an experience bag of 10 years offering a mix of academic, research and administrative portfolios. She is presently working as Assistant Professor | Director Local Quality Enhancement Cell Law| at NUST Law School. She is also the focal person for harassment. She has taught in International Islamic University, Bahria University Islamabad and liaised with Legal industry and international stakeholders for MOUs and academic and industry linkages. She has been the Focal Person for Disability; ensuring compliance of Institutional Disability Policies with national mandate. As an individual living with albinism, she brings a personal perspective to questions of inclusion, representation, and human dignity in law. She is interested in legal discourse on Diversity )
/Pg 112 0 R
/K [0]
>>
