/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 662 0 R
/E (The relationship between Pakistan and Russia has experienced a notable transformation in light of emerging geo-economic paradigms. Given the widening global divide and the rise of a multipolar hegemony, it is essential to reassess the dynamics of these bilateral relations from a modern perspective. This research proposes a comprehensive policy framework to enhance Pakistan-Russia relations by establishing institutional partnerships. Furthermore, this study delineates the collaborative principles and foundational pillars, along with critical policy imperatives, necessary to foster this cooperation. The framework is conceptualized as a layered schematic, commencing with foundational policy principles: sovereign equality, mutual benefits, transparency, inclusive partnership, and sustainability, which serve as the guiding tenets for equitable and enduring collaboration. This study builds on the framework established by the 10th Intergovernmental Commission \(November 25-27, 2025\) and incorporates elements from the forthcoming 2030 Economic Cooperation Program. It outlines collaborative principles across six core policy pillars: tourism and regional connectivity; language and vocational skill development; capacity building for knowledge corridors; innovation and technology transfer; trade facilitation; and regulatory harmonization. The engagement of various stakeholders is emphasized, promoting a multi-sectoral approach. Policy analysis and reviews integrate multiple sectoral assessments through a regional information pool, with a strategic focus on regional sustainability. This leads to the development of policies driven by national initiatives in trade, customs, technology transfer, and human resource development and exchange. Our findings would be useful for policymakers, government officials, and special interest groups for policy analysis and design.)
/Pg 113 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
