/P 664 0 R
/E (Between the 2010s and 2020s, Russia and Pakistan expanded institutional formats for bilateral cooperation. Despite this, the level of trade, economic, and investment cooperation remains limited. The report examines the potential for using multilateral formats to develop bilateral cooperation, primarily the SCO, of which Pakistan has been a full member since 2017, and BRICS+, which it may soon join. It analyzes the potential for cooperation in energy, transport, and humanitarian exchanges, as well as factors hindering deeper cooperation, including low economic interdependence and limited implementation of existing agreements.)
/Pg 115 0 R
/K [4]
>>
