/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 667 0 R
/E (Russia's interaction with friendly countries and partnerships in higher education and scientific research are becoming increasingly important and serve as a tool for the economic development of countries that learn and innovate together. This report explores the potential and possibilities for partnership between Russia and Pakistan in educational and scientific fields. It aims to analyze the current state of scientific and educational interaction between the two countries, identify priority areas for further partnership, and propose practical steps to strengthen integration processes. Particular attention should be paid to the use of space technologies to address priority issues such as improving industrial and environmental safety, digital transformation of industries, and ensuring technological sovereignty.Formats of interaction:- Academic mobility: the implementation of joint educational programs and internships promotes intercultural dialogue and expands the international experience of educational participants;- Joint scientific projects: the establishment of joint research centers and laboratories will enable the effective development of innovative technologies, stimulating the economic and technological development of both countries;- Training world-class personnel: the joint efforts of universities will help prepare qualified personnel capable of implementing space projects. The involvement of educational institutions and scientific organizations in Russia and Pakistan in international cooperation initiatives, including within the framework of the Shanghai Cooperation Organization \(SCO\), is highly significant. The Russian Ministry of Education and Science places particular emphasis on supporting such cooperation by providing grants for joint scientific research. A range of promising areas of cooperation can be identified with the participation of the Roscosmos Constellation consortium, which unites Russian universities successfully implementing training programs for the rocket and space industry, as well as within the framework of the Russian Ministry of Education and Science's federal project "Personnel for Space" \(2026-2030\), aimed at developing a comprehensive system for training highly qualified specialists for the rocket and space industry. Thus, the synergy between the scientific and educational resources of Russia and Pakistan can strengthen long-term international cooperation, increase the competitiveness of national economies, and contribute to solving current global technological challenges.)
/Pg 118 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
