/E (Dr. Ayesha Ashfaq is an Assistant Professor at the School of Integrated Social Sciences, University of Lahore, Punjab, Pakistan. She holds a Ph.D. and an M.Phil. in South Asian Studies from the University of the Punjab, Lahore. She completed the Gaming for Peace \(G4P\) Fellowship at the Center for Security, Strategy, and Policy Research \(CSSPR\), University of Lahore, Pakistan. With extensive experience in academic and research activities, her research interests include political and sociocultural issues in Pakistan and India, communal politics, ethnic conflicts in South Asia, violence and human rights, minority issues, extremism, SAARC Pakistan-Russia Relation, and CPEC.)
/Pg 121 0 R
/K [0]
