/E (Ahmed Osama Tahir is a PhD Scholar in International Relations and a Faculty Member in the Department of International Relations at Federal Urdu University of Arts, Science and Technology, Pakistan. He is an educator, researcher, Presidential Award achiever, professional trainer, and social activist. His 13 years of professional career include key leadership roles such as Program Consultant with various international NGOs, including RELO, U.S. Embassy Islamabad. He also has expertise in international business collaborations, actively promoting entrepreneurship, youth development, and geopolitical engagement. Co- author, Memona Mujahid, is a PhD scholar in Linguistics and a faculty member at the Department of English, International Islamic University, )
