/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 671 0 R
/E (Although the diplomatic relations between Russia and Pakistan have been evolving in terms of trade, energy, and security, the language barrier remains a major challenge to enhancing bilateral cooperation. This study explores the significance of Russian language education in Pakistan as a strategic tool to strengthen cultural ties, geopolitical, educational, and economic cooperation between the two countries. Existing scholarship emphasizes the urgent need for language diplomacy and policy for refined negotiation and prolonged collaboration. This research fills the identified gap by examining how the study of the Russian language in Pakistan offers opportunities to enhance diplomatic communications and geopolitical coordination. The investigation has followed an interdisciplinary approach employing Neoliberal Institutionalism \(Joseph Nye, 1990\) and Soft Power Theory \(Robert Kohane, 1984\) of International Relations, together with the Sociocognitive theory of Intercultural Pragmatics \(Istvan Kecskes, 2014\). The researchers conducted the interviews with educators and students from the Department of Russian, National University of Modern Languages, Islamabad, Pakistan \(NUML\), and the diplomats from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the Russian Embassy in Pakistan. The study concludes that in Pakistan, though the Russian language courses are increasingly becoming popular, they are not fully incorporated into the diplomatic strategy. The efficacy of language learning as a deeper expansion of geopolitical and economic engagement is obstructed by the linguistic gap, inadequate training material, and the absence of consensus between the education framework and the foreign policy agendas. The research suggests developing a strategic framework to incorporate language education into foreign policy as well as international relations practice. The study offers valuable policy recommendations to diplomats and educators, emphasizing the need for a coordinated language diplomacy to enhance geopolitical cooperation and strengthen educational and economic ties between the two nations.)
/Pg 122 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
