/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 676 0 R
/E (This paper provides a comparative study of paradiplomacy the international activities of subnational entities within the federal structures of Pakistan and the Russian Federation. It examines the legal frameworks and political mechanisms that allow regions, such as Tatarstan in Russia and provinces like Punjab or Sindh in Pakistan, to engage in independent foreign economic and cultural cooperation. By identifying common challenges and unique regional strategies, the research highlights how sub-state diplomacy can complement national foreign policy goals and foster direct bilateral ties between the two nations' diverse regions.)
/Pg 127 0 R
/K [3]
>>
