/E (This research explores the historical development of the Persian poetic tradition within the Indian subcontinent, focusing on the unique synthesis of "Sabk-e-Hindi" \(the Indian style\). it examines the linguistic and cultural dialogue between Persian literary norms and local Indian traditions, analyzing how this interaction transformed classical genres and metaphors. By tracing these cross-cultural influences, the study highlights the role of the Persian language as a bridge for intellectual and aesthetic exchange across the Eastern Islamic world. )
/Pg 130 0 R
/K [3]
>>
