/E (This research examines the historical evolution and cultural identity of Christianity in Pakistan, from colonial missionary roots to its current minority status. It analyzes how the community navigates the socio-political pressures of state Islamization while maintaining its unique religious and social traditions. By exploring the intersection of faith and the Pakistani social fabric, the study highlights the resilience and evolving role of Christians within the nation's contemporary landscape.)
