20523 0 obj
<<
/Title (compatibility of the infrastructure and regulatory uncertainty as a result of the sanctions on the utilization of routes through the structured survey of the participants of the logistics business of about 80-100 cross-border actors \(along with targeted interviews with the experts\). It examines whether logistics reliability itself serves as a mediating factor between trade decision and connectedness. Based on the trade facilitation and logistics performance models, the findings suggest that firms rationally minimize shipment frequency or avoid routes entirely when shipment delivery times cannot be predicted, border processes are unreliable, and the rules are ambiguous, regardless of the presence of the routes. Drawing scale-based evidence at the firm level, it refocuses the attention on infrastructure expansion and the performance and coordination of corridors, and it outlines the policy priorities in the cooperation of customs and trade facilitation, as well as the governance of corridors needed to promote sustainable Russia-Pakistan economic integration.)
/Dest [35 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 20519 0 R
>>
endobj
