/Title (This article analyzes Pakistan's efforts to bring its national financial system into compliance with Sharia law. It examines the theory and history of this issue, the current situation, and prospects for cooperation between Pakistan and Russia in light of the Russian Federation's federal law on a pilot project for partner financing.)
/Dest [77 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 20530 0 R
>>
endobj
20535 0 obj
<<
/Title (Cryptocurrencies, thanks to their ideological and technological foundation, are developing in a decentralized manner, bringing together individuals in an ecosystem seeking effective solutions to their problems using new technologies. This gives rise to new financial instruments, data storage platforms, and distributed networks for tracking logistics and the authenticity of goods. Scaling processes requires a legal framework capable of covering all types of activities present in the country. The problem arises when government agencies limit themselves to planning legislation only within the country, as digital technologies operate internationally. It is necessary to synchronize the legal framework between countries seeking to collaborate in various economic sectors that utilize cryptocurrencies in their activities. This article examines: The current legal reality in Russia and Pakistan, including which authorities are responsible for regulating and managing the markets where cryptocurrencies are used. It is necessary to review draft laws and current legislation, and where the definitions and general rules for working with cryptocurrencies converge and diverge. The state of the cryptocurrency market in each country, which projects are being created to address current societal problems, and opportunities for collaboration between these projects. An analysis of the strengths and weaknesses of each country is needed to identify the most effective collaborations between projects. An opportunity for cooperation within legal, academic, and corporate frameworks to strengthen ties between countries and promote domestic solutions in the crypto sphere. The goal of this work is to describe the common reality in each country and propose the best paths for further development to avoid lagging behind international trends and to bring national projects and governing bodies closer together, increasing their effectiveness both locally and internationally. Reports and articles may be submitted in either Russian or English; this will be subject to the conference organizers' approval.)
/Dest [36 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 20532 0 R
>>
endobj
