20543 0 obj
<<
/Title (The Impact of Globalization on Innovative Interaction between the Economic Systems of Russia and Pakistan)
/Dest [76 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 20547 0 R
/Next 20540 0 R
>>
endobj
20544 0 obj
<<
/Title (A characteristic of the development of the modern global economy is the gradual and relatively stable division of countries into core capitalist economies and peripheral economies. While industrial production processes gradually shifted, in terms of location and growth of economic efficiency, to countries with cheap labor and economic resources, core capitalist countries have made the development of innovation, the development and sale of new technological solutions and production methods on the global market, the foundation of their economic systems. The globalization processes occurring in the global economy in recent decades have only intensified this trend.Nevertheless, a number of new centers of innovation, scientific, and financial development worldwide demonstrate that peripheral countries are aware of the current situation and are taking steps to change it. The development and formation of new innovation centers requires government action within the framework of national economic and innovation policies. However, existing and growing trends toward regionalization in the global economic system demonstrate that the combined efforts of countries to create conditions for the development of new technological solutions \(within groups of countries\) are proving most effective.In accordance with the above, it is important to consider that innovative interaction requires both collaboration between innovative and manufacturing organizations and cooperation between countries through the establishment of links between scientific and educational systems. Accordingly, cooperation in scientific and educational spheres becomes the foundation for future innovative interaction.Innovative interaction between the economic systems of the Russian Federation and Pakistan can only be based on the establishment of information \(communication\) links between scientific, educational, financial, and manufacturing structures. Each level of this systemic interaction is important, both within regional economic systems and at the level of national economies as a whole. Selecting priority areas of interaction, taking into account the scientific and financial capabilities of the two countries, requires analyzing and forecasting various options.)
/Dest [76 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 20540 0 R
>>
endobj
20545 0 obj
<<
/Title (This article examines the institutional foundations and strategic trajectories of economic integration between the Russian Federation and the Islamic Republic of Pakistan within the broader context of Eurasian cooperation. Despite a historically modest economic relationship, recent geopolitical shifts and mutual strategic interests have catalyzed a renewed impetus for bilateral engagement. This paper analyzes the evolving models of trade and investment cooperation, moving beyond ad-hoc interactions toward a more structured partnership. It investigates the core drivers of integration, including energy complementarity, infrastructure development, and shared aspirations for a multipolar world order. Concurrently, it identifies critical institutional deficits, such as the absence of a Bilateral Investment Treaty \(BIT\) and the disruptive impact of Western sanctions, which impede progress. By examining flagship projects like the Pakistan Stream gas pipeline and railway modernization initiatives, the article assesses the efficacy of existing institutional mechanisms, including the Intergovernmental Commission \(IGC\). The findings suggest that while a strong political foundation exists, translating this into substantial economic integration requires the creation of resilient financial architectures, harmonized legal frameworks, and the successful implementation of pilot projects to build trust and demonstrate viability.)
/Dest [37 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 20542 0 R
>>
endobj
