20666 0 obj
<<
/Title (Intensification of Russian-Pakistani Relations in the context of regional consolidation.)
/Dest [62 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 20669 0 R
/Next 20662 0 R
>>
endobj
20667 0 obj
<<
/Title (The historical and geopolitical analysis of the Russian-Pakistani relations reveals that, although Pakistan has traditionally not occupied a significant place in the foreign policy of the Russian Federation, this fact in the current scenario of the global transformation and transition to a Polycentric world does not negate the importance of strengthening relations between Moscow and Islamabad due to their shared regional interests. Actually, both two countries are actively engaged in the creation of the strong dialogue architecture at all levels, including the highest one. In this context, it is worth mentioning the official visit of the Pakistan Prime-Minister Shehbaz Sharif to Moscow on June, 2026, which is expected to be a breakthrough in the bilateral relations. Moreover, during the ceremony of presenting credentials by the new Ambassador of the Islamic Republic of Pakistan H.E. Mr. Faisal Niaz Tirmizi to the President of Russia on January 15, 2026 Vladimir Putin underlined with satisfaction the "truly mutually beneficial" relations between Russia and Pakistan with their close cooperation not only on bilateral, but also on the multilateral levels, as the SCO full-fledged members, with the great economic, technological and human potential of this largest regional Organization. It seems, that the main areas of Russia-Pakistan relations in the vector of the regional integration, according to the priorities ranking, include cooperation in the following 3 important areas: - transport and energy connectivity; - fight against terrorism; - elimination of drug trafficking. Thus, the regional connectivity has practically become the main driver of their bilateral interaction gradually reaching a new level of mutually beneficial partnership as a reflection of both states involvement in the creation of the joint economic and security structure of the Greater Eurasia. Their progress on this track has been facilitated by the coordinated implementation of the Russian integration project EAEU- BEP with the conjunctive project OBOR/BRI-CPEC, which opens the prospects to the global routes access of BRICS, where Pakistan in November 2023 officially applied for the membership.)
/Dest [62 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 20662 0 R
>>
endobj
