20706 0 obj
<<
/Title (The influence of the American factor on the development of Russian-Pakistani relations in the 21st century)
/Dest [58 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 20709 0 R
/Next 20702 0 R
>>
endobj
20707 0 obj
<<
/Title (Relations between Russia and Pakistan have undergone a complex journey from the antagonism of the Cold War to a modern pragmatic partnership. Signs of gradual rapprochement began to emerge in the early 21st century, when Pakistan, a historical US and NATO ally, began seeking to diversify its international ties, allowing Russia to expand its influence in South Asia. The changing global geopolitical architecture, particularly the emergence of a multipolar world and the shift of the global economic center of gravity to Asia, created fertile ground for Russian-Pakistani rapprochement. In the 21st century, Pakistan strives to chart an independent course on the global political stage, and to this end, it is making significant efforts to strengthen national economic and political stability. At the same time, like many countries in the Global South, it faces significant pressure on its political position in the face of great power competition. The rapprochement between Russia and Pakistan poses a complex challenge for US foreign policy in the 21st century. The US factor remains critical for the development of intensive cooperation between Pakistan and Russia. US sanctions against Russian companies have frozen major projects, in particular the Pakistan Stream gas pipeline, the agreement for which was signed in 2015. If US sanctions against Russia are lifted, Pakistan will gain strategic space to strengthen economic relations with Russia, particularly in securing long-term energy deals at competitive prices, which will significantly benefit the Pakistani economy. Despite American opposition, over the past two decades, political relations between Pakistan and Russia have improved, and mechanisms for the gradual expansion of trade and economic cooperation have emerged. Pakistan is a potentially major market for Russian goods and services, particularly in the energy and engineering sectors. Pakistan's accession to the Shanghai Cooperation Organization \(SCO\) in 2017, of which Russia is a key member, was a significant milestone, providing a platform for multilateral cooperation and further impetus for bilateral ties.)
/Dest [58 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 20702 0 R
>>
endobj
